<%
  var pageUrl = siteUrl + '/free-invoice-generator-india';
  var checked = '10 November 2026';
  var ex = example, exd = exampleData;
  var SRC = {
    rule46: 'https://taxinformation.cbic.gov.in/content/html/tax_repository/gst/rules/cgst_rules/active/chapter6/rule46_v1.00.html',
    rule47: 'https://taxinformation.cbic.gov.in/content/html/tax_repository/gst/rules/cgst_rules/active/chapter6/rule47_v1.00.html',
    rule48: 'https://taxinformation.cbic.gov.in/content/html/tax_repository/gst/rules/cgst_rules/active/chapter6/rule48_v1.00.html',
    rule49: 'https://taxinformation.cbic.gov.in/content/html/tax_repository/gst/rules/cgst_rules/active/chapter6/rule49_v1.00.html',
    rule34: 'https://taxinformation.cbic.gov.in/content/html/tax_repository/gst/rules/cgst_rules/active/chapter4/rule34_v1.00.html',
    rule96a: 'https://taxinformation.cbic.gov.in/content/html/tax_repository/gst/rules/cgst_rules/active/chapter10/rule96a_v1.00.html',
    act: 'https://taxinformation.cbic.gov.in/content/html/tax_repository/gst/acts/2017_CGST_act/documents/Central_Goods_and_Services_Tax_Act__2017_28-September-2022.html',
    hsn: 'https://www.gstcouncil.gov.in/sites/default/files/2024-05/notfctn-78-central-tax-english-2020.pdf',
    registration: 'https://gstcouncil.gov.in/sites/default/files/e-version-gst-flyers/Registration_under_GST_Law_new.pdf',
    rates2025: 'https://static.pib.gov.in/WriteReadData/specificdocs/documents/2025/sep/doc202594628401.pdf',
    council57: 'https://static.pib.gov.in/WriteReadData/specificdocs/documents/2026/oct/doc_10142_20261009_21430401.pdf',
    einvMandate: 'https://einvoice6.gst.gov.in/content/e-invoice-mandate/',
    einv30: 'https://einvoice6.gst.gov.in/content/revised-time-limit-for-e-invoice-reporting-for-businesses-with-aato-of-%E2%82%B910-crores-above/'
  };
  var faqs = [
    ['What must a GST invoice in India include?', 'For a tax invoice, Rule 46 of the CGST Rules, 2017 lists: the supplier\'s name, address and GSTIN; a consecutive serial number of up to 16 characters, unique for the financial year; the date; the recipient\'s name, address and GSTIN if registered; the HSN code of goods or SAC of services; a description; quantity and unit; the total and the taxable value after discount; the rate and amount of central, State or UT, and integrated tax; the place of supply for inter-State supplies; whether tax is payable on reverse charge; and a signature or digital signature.'],
    ['What is the difference between CGST, SGST and IGST?', 'When the supplier and the place of supply are in the same State or Union territory, the GST is split into CGST (to the Centre) and SGST or UTGST (to the State or Union territory), each at half the rate. When the place of supply is in another State, the supply carries IGST at the full rate. The invoice shows whichever applies on each line.'],
    ['What are the GST rates in India now?', 'Since 22 September 2025 most goods and services are taxed at 5% or 18%, a 40% rate applies to items such as tobacco, aerated drinks and luxury goods, and some supplies are exempt. The rate depends on the HSN or SAC code, so look yours up in the CBIC rate notifications.'],
    ['Do I need a GSTIN to issue a GST invoice?', 'Yes. Only a registered person issues a tax invoice and charges GST, and it must show the supplier\'s GSTIN. If you are below the registration limit and not registered, you cannot charge GST: issue a bill of supply or an ordinary invoice without tax.'],
    ['How many digits must the HSN code have?', 'Under Notification 78/2020-CT, 4 digits if your aggregate turnover in the previous financial year was up to ₹5 crore, and 6 digits if it was above ₹5 crore. A supplier with turnover up to ₹5 crore need not show the digits on invoices to unregistered recipients.'],
    ['How long can an invoice number be?', 'At most 16 characters. Rule 46(b) allows letters, numerals, a hyphen and a slash, in one or more series, and the number must be unique for the financial year (1 April to 31 March).'],
    ['Within how many days must I issue the invoice?', 'For services, within 30 days of the supply, or 45 days for an insurer, bank or other financial institution including an NBFC (Rule 47). For goods, before or at the time the goods are removed or delivered (section 31 of the CGST Act).'],
    ['Is an invoice from this page an e-invoice?', 'No. An e-invoice carries an Invoice Reference Number and a QR code from the government Invoice Registration Portal. Businesses with aggregate turnover above ₹5 crore in any year since 2017-18 must issue invoices that way. Below that limit, a signed invoice like the one this page makes is how you invoice.'],
    ['How do I invoice a client outside India?', 'Choose an export option. The invoice then carries the endorsement Rule 46 sets, the recipient\'s name and address, the delivery address and the country of destination. You either export under a bond or Letter of Undertaking without paying IGST, or pay IGST and claim it back as a refund.']
  ];
